  "notes": "Source: Florida A&M University 2022-2023 General Catalog, official degree planner 'Computer Science, BS' (ABET CAC-accredited program), transcribed term-by-term on 2026-09-30: https://catalog.famu.edu/preview_degree_planner.php?catoid=11&poid=3448&returnto=935&print . Degree/program name verified against FAMU's official Degree and Majors Inventory and All Programs listing (famu.edu/academics/all-programs): 'Bachelor of Science in Computer Science' (BS), College of Science and Technology. A current-catalog (2025-2026) CS degree planner was searched for but only this 2022-2023 planner is published; catalog_year reflects the actual source. Transcription method: all course codes and titles verbatim from the planner (including 'FIRST YEAR EXPRIENCE' and 'General Physics II w/Lab*'). The planner prints per-term totals (17/16/14/15/17/17/12/12) and 'Total: 120'; credits not printed per-course were forced from the planner's own printed term totals and cross-checked: BSC 1005C=4, COP 3014C=4 (confirmed 4 cr at FAMU on the official FAMU-FSU engineering curriculum page), COP 3330=3, COP 3530=3, PHY 2048=4 (confirmed on FAMU's official Physics Curriculum Map in the catalog.famu.edu media library), PHY 2049 lecture=4 with PHY 2049L=1 (the planner's '(5)' is the combined lecture+lab block), CDA 3101C=3, CIS 4250=3, CDA 4102=3, CIS 4301=3. The transcribed sequence sums to exactly the planner's published 120 total -- no discrepancy. Caveats: (1) This is the catalog's sample term-by-term sequence; social science/humanities/general electives, the two department-approved math courses, and major electives vary by student. (2) Departmental approved math courses for this curriculum (per planner): MAD 3401 Numerical Analysis, MAS 3105 Linear Algebra, STA 2023 Introduction to Probability and Statistics I (3 cr each). (3) Prerequisites are included ONLY where stated in official FAMU catalog materials -- COT 3100 (catalog course description: MAC 2311), COT 3101 (catalog: COT 3100), COT 4210 (catalog: COT 3101 and COP 2532), CIS 4301 (official CIS Curriculum Map milestone: COP 3530 and COP 3710). All other prereq arrays are empty rather than invented. (4) COP 2532 is in external_prereqs because the catalog lists it as a COT 4210 prerequisite, though it is not part of the sample sequence (the sequence's data-structures course is COP 3530). (5) FAMU's Cybersecurity curriculum map notes COP 3014C normally requires MAC 1105 with C or better; students placing directly into MAC 2311 do not need it.",
